From 1e86d1b409563b2b4f3c3d5adddc17d29aca4456 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 11:05:49 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 74/79] kosmickrisp: keep the ballot workaround on Apple7 and
 Apple8

KK_WORKAROUND_3 routes every ballot and vote through simd_or, because Metal's
simd_ballot, quad_any and quad_all answer for every thread the SIMD group
entered the shader with rather than the threads active where the call sits.
The block that retires workarounds on macOS 27 clears the whole first seven,
so an Apple7 or Apple8 GPU loses it as soon as the operating system is new
enough, and the workaround's own entry already names the test that then fails:
dEQP-VK.subgroups.shader_quad_control.divergent_condition.

The test puts subgroupQuadAny and subgroupQuadAll inside a condition that only
part of each 2x2 quad satisfies, and checks that the votes saw exactly the
invocations that entered. On an Apple7 GPU under macOS 27.0 (build 26A428) the
native quad votes answer for the whole quad instead, so a fragment whose quad
partners did not enter still reads its partners' values and the green channel
comes out set where the test requires it clear. The same entry lists
dEQP-VK.subgroups.ballot_other.*.subgroupballotfindlsb and
dEQP-VK.subgroups.arithmetic.graphics.* for the simd_ballot form of the defect.

This is the shape KK_WORKAROUND_4 already has: a defect the operating system
cannot resolve because it is in the silicon, blanket-retired by a version
check that only knows about the operating system. Carve the ballot workaround
out of the retired set on Apple family eight and below alongside it, and
retire the rest as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 docs/drivers/kosmickrisp/workarounds.rst |  9 +++++++++
 src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_device.c       | 12 +++++++-----
 2 files changed, 16 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/drivers/kosmickrisp/workarounds.rst b/docs/drivers/kosmickrisp/workarounds.rst
index 8d672860..ef37fc4c 100644
--- a/docs/drivers/kosmickrisp/workarounds.rst
+++ b/docs/drivers/kosmickrisp/workarounds.rst
@@ -508,10 +508,19 @@ Alternatively, the conditional can be changed to include ``simd_ballot(true)``:
       temp = 2u;
 
 
+Because the defect is in the silicon, an operating system release cannot
+resolve it there: the workaround is therefore kept on Apple7 and Apple8 GPUs
+whatever version the operating system reports.
+
 | Log:
 | 2025-09-09: Workaround implemented and reported to Apple
 | 2026-04-28: Workaround updated to expand to all ballot/vote ops.
 | 2026-06-22: Fixed in macOS 27 Beta (Build 26A5353q)
+| 2026-09-14: Still reproduces on an Apple7 GPU under macOS 27.0 (build
+  26A428), where ``quad_all`` and ``quad_any`` reached inside a conditional
+  answer for every thread the SIMD group entered the shader with and
+  ``dEQP-VK.subgroups.shader_quad_control.divergent_condition`` fails; kept
+  for Apple7 and Apple8
 
 KK_WORKAROUND_2
 ---------------
diff --git a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_device.c b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_device.c
index f4c61695..4a8f20b4 100644
--- a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_device.c
+++ b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_device.c
@@ -245,15 +245,17 @@ kk_parse_device_environment_options(struct kk_device *dev)
       dev->disabled_workarounds |= BITFIELD64_BIT(index);
    }
 
-   /* Workarounds resolved on macOS 27.  KK_WORKAROUND_4 is not one of them on
-    * every GPU: it compensates for Apple7 and Apple8 silicon, where
-    * simd_is_helper_thread() does not observe a discard_fragment() that ran
-    * before it, so the query stays unusable there whatever the operating
+   /* Workarounds resolved on macOS 27.  KK_WORKAROUND_3 and KK_WORKAROUND_4
+    * are not among them on every GPU: both compensate for Apple7 and Apple8
+    * silicon, where simd_is_helper_thread() does not observe a
+    * discard_fragment() that ran before it and a ballot or vote inside a
+    * conditional block answers for every thread the SIMD group entered the
+    * shader with.  Neither query becomes usable there whatever the operating
     * system reports. */
    if (ns_is_os_version_at_least(27, 0, 0)) {
       uint64_t resolved = BITFIELD64_MASK(7) | BITFIELD64_BIT(12);
       if (kk_device_physical(dev)->info.gpu_apple_family <= 8u)
-         resolved &= ~BITFIELD64_BIT(4);
+         resolved &= ~(BITFIELD64_BIT(3) | BITFIELD64_BIT(4));
       dev->disabled_workarounds |= resolved;
    }
 }
